{"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"tokens":[{"text":"final","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"class","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MultipleFontCompositeSemanticToken","kind":"identifier"}],"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["macOS"]}]},{"content":[{"level":2,"text":"Overview","type":"heading","anchor":"overview"},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["        \/\/ Assuming in Figma with have a font semantic token displayLarge,","        \/\/ with values depending to size class. These values are defined as font composite raw tokens.","        let bold850 = FontCompositeSemanticToken(size: size850, lineHeight: lineHeight1050, weight: weight700, letterSpacing: letterSpacing850)","        let bold1450 = FontCompositeSemanticToken(size: size1450, lineHeight: lineHeight1850, weight: weight700, letterSpacing: letterSpacing1450)","","        \/\/ Then the develoment team declares an \"higher\" level font semantic token","        \/\/ inside FontCompositeSemanticTokens protocol,","        \/\/ and defined inside OrangeTheme+FontCompositeSemanticTokens extension","        var displayLarge: MultipleFontCompositeSemanticToken {","            MultipleFontCompositeSemanticToken(compact: bold850, regular: bold1450)","        }","","        \/\/ If the same font is used whatever the size class is","        var displayLarge: MultipleFontCompositeSemanticToken { MultipleFontCompositeSemanticToken(bold650) }","","        \/\/ The theme exposes both generated elevation semantic tokens and \"crafted\" higher level elevation semantic tokens.","        \/\/ It is recommended to use the higher level version as it is less error-prone."]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The case of this ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/OUDSTokensSemantic\/documentation\/OUDSTokensSemantic\/MultipleFontCompositeSemanticToken","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" is quite particular because in fact it contains ","type":"text"},{"code":"FontCompositeSemanticToken","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(i.e. raw tokens) instead of semantic tokens.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"In fact there is not “font composite semantic tokens” defined in the ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Figma","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" kit.","type":"text"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"0.22.0","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"type":"aside","name":"Since","style":"note"}],"kind":"content"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Kind of semantic tokens which will wrap a combination of "},{"code":"FontCompositeSemanticToken","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" depending to size classes."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Kind of composite token with multiple values, but not named “composite” because this word is already used in the design system."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Allows to gather the multiple-value tokens from "},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Figma"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":" inside one object."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"If a font token exists with its value depending to the size class, it must be packed in such "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/OUDSTokensSemantic\/documentation\/OUDSTokensSemantic\/MultipleFontCompositeSemanticToken"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/OUDSTokensSemantic\/documentation\/OUDSTokensSemantic"]]},"kind":"symbol","variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/oudstokenssemantic\/multiplefontcompositesemantictoken"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"topicSections":[{"anchor":"Operators","title":"Operators","identifiers":["doc:\/\/OUDSTokensSemantic\/documentation\/OUDSTokensSemantic\/MultipleFontCompositeSemanticToken\/_(_:_:)"],"generated":true},{"anchor":"Initializers","title":"Initializers","identifiers":["doc